#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:68 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:68
msgid "Opening Image"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:70 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:70
msgid ""
"A snapshot of the hero's world before the story changes it, setting the tone "
"of the film."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:76 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:76
msgid "Theme Stated"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:78 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:78
msgid ""
"Someone, usually not the hero, says what the story is really about: the "
"lesson the hero will have to learn."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:84 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:84
msgid "Set-Up"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:86 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:86
msgid ""
"The hero's ordinary life, their flaws and what's missing from it, and the "
"people who will matter later."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:92 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:92
msgid "Catalyst"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:94 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:94
msgid ""
"The event that knocks the hero's world off balance: a telegram, a death, a "
"chance meeting."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:100 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:100
msgid "Debate"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:102 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:102
msgid "The hero doubts, resists or prepares: should they go? Can they?"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:108 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:108
msgid "Break into Two"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:110 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:110
msgid ""
"The hero chooses to act, leaving the old world for the upside-down world of "
"Act Two."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:116 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:116
msgid "B Story"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:118 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:118
msgid ""
"A new relationship, often a love story or mentor, that carries the theme and "
"helps the hero learn it."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:124 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:124
msgid "Fun and Games"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:126 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:126
msgid ""
"The promise of the premise: the scenes the audience came to see, the hero "
"exploring the new world."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:132 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:225
#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:132 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:225
msgid "Midpoint"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:134 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:134
msgid ""
"A false victory or a false defeat. The stakes are raised and the fun and "
"games are over."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:140 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:140
msgid "Bad Guys Close In"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:142 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:142
msgid ""
"The enemies regroup, doubt and jealousy split the hero's team, and things "
"get steadily worse."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:148 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:148
msgid "All Is Lost"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:150 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:150
msgid ""
"The lowest point, the opposite of the midpoint. Something or someone dies, "
"if only an old way of thinking."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:156 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:156
msgid "Dark Night of the Soul"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:158 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:158
msgid ""
"The hero mourns what's lost and hits bottom, until they find the last idea "
"that will save them."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:164 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:164
msgid "Break into Three"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:166 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:166
msgid ""
"The answer, found by bringing the A and B stories together. The hero chooses "
"to fight."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:172 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:172
msgid "Finale"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:174 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:174
msgid ""
"The hero puts the lesson into practice, beats the bad guys and changes the "
"world for the better."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:180 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:180
msgid "Final Image"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:182 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:182
msgid "The opposite of the opening image: proof that change has happened."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:193 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:193
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:195 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:195
msgid ""
"The protagonist, their world and what they want, before anything goes wrong."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:201 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:201
msgid "Inciting Incident"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:203 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:203
msgid ""
"The event that upsets the protagonist's life and sets the story in motion."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:209 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:209
msgid "Plot Point One"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:211 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:211
msgid ""
"About a quarter in. The protagonist commits to the goal and there's no going "
"back. End of Act One."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:217 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:217
msgid "Rising Action"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:219 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:219
msgid ""
"The protagonist pursues the goal against growing obstacles, allies and "
"enemies take shape."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:227 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:227
msgid ""
"Halfway. A reversal or revelation that raises the stakes and changes how the "
"protagonist goes after the goal."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:233 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:233
msgid "Complications"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:235 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:235
msgid ""
"Pressure builds from outside and within, and the cost of failure keeps "
"rising."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:241 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:241
msgid "Plot Point Two"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:243 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:243
msgid ""
"About three quarters in. A crisis or the lowest point that forces a final "
"decision. End of Act Two."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:249 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:249
msgid "Climax"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:251 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:251
msgid ""
"The protagonist confronts the central conflict head on, and wins or loses."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:257 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:257
msgid "Resolution"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:259 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:259
msgid "The aftermath: loose ends tied up and a new normal for the protagonist."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:270 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:270
msgid "You"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:271 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:271
msgid "1. A character is in a zone of comfort."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:275 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:275
msgid "Need"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:276 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:276
msgid "2. But they want something."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:280 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:280
msgid "Go"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:281 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:281
msgid "3. They enter an unfamiliar situation."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:286 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:286
msgid "4. They adapt to it."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:290 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:290
msgid "Find"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:291 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:291
msgid "5. They get what they wanted."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:295 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:295
msgid "Take"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:296 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:296
msgid "6. They pay a heavy price for it."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:300 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:300
msgid "Return"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:301 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:301
msgid "7. Then they return to their familiar situation."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:306 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:306
msgid "8. Having changed."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:315 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:315
msgid "Sequence A: Status Quo and Inciting Incident"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:317 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:317
msgid ""
"The protagonist's world and what they want, ending with the inciting "
"incident."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:323 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:323
msgid "Sequence B: Predicament and Lock-In"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:325 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:325
msgid ""
"The protagonist wrestles with the new situation, ending when they're locked "
"into the story's main tension. End of Act One."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:332 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:332
msgid "Sequence C: First Obstacle"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:334 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:334
msgid ""
"The first attempt to solve the problem, the easy way, which fails and raises "
"the stakes."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:340 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:340
msgid "Sequence D: First Culmination"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:342 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:342
msgid ""
"A bigger attempt, ending at the midpoint with a glimpse of how things could "
"end."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:348 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:348
msgid "Sequence E: Subplot and Rising Action"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:350 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:350
msgid ""
"The consequences of the midpoint, subplots come to the fore, things get "
"harder."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:356 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:356
msgid "Sequence F: Main Culmination"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:358 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:358
msgid ""
"The main tension is resolved, often at the protagonist's lowest point. End "
"of Act Two."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:364 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:364
msgid "Sequence G: New Tension and Twist"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:366 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:366
msgid ""
"A new tension carries the story to the end, with a twist that upends "
"expectations."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:372 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:372
msgid "Sequence H: Resolution"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:374 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:374
msgid ""
"The climax and its aftermath: the story's questions answered and loose ends "
"tied up."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:385 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:385
msgid "Mini-Movie 1: The Setup"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:387 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:387
msgid ""
"Hook the audience, show the hero's world, and end on the inciting incident. "
"Each mini-movie has its own beginning, middle and end, and closes on a "
"question that pulls into the next."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:395 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:395
msgid "Mini-Movie 2: The Lock-In"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:397 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:397
msgid ""
"The hero is drawn in until there's no way out, ending on the decision that "
"starts Act Two."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:403 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:403
msgid "Mini-Movie 3: The First Trial"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:405 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:405
msgid "A new world and the first try at the goal, ending in a setback."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:411 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:411
msgid "Mini-Movie 4: The Midpoint"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:413 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:413
msgid ""
"Things build to a big reversal at the midpoint that changes the hero's "
"course."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:419 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:419
msgid "Mini-Movie 5: The Complications"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:421 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:421
msgid ""
"Fallout from the midpoint, subplots tighten and the opposition hits back."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:427 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:427
msgid "Mini-Movie 6: The Lowest Point"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:429 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:429
msgid "Everything falls apart, ending with all hope lost. End of Act Two."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:435 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:435
msgid "Mini-Movie 7: The Twist"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:437 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:437
msgid ""
"The hero regroups with a new plan, and a twist raises the stakes one last "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:443 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:443
msgid "Mini-Movie 8: The Climax"
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:445 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:445
msgid "The final confrontation and the new world it leaves behind."
msgstr ""

#: trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:454 trelby/screenplay/beatsheets.py:454
msgid "Save the Cat"
msgstr ""

